    "text": "To determine how many times Enrique will need to shred 6 units of paper until all of his 2,132 contracts are shredded, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of pages in all the contracts:**\n   Each contract is 132 pages long, and Enrique has 2,132 contracts.\n   \\[\n   2132 \\times 132 = 283,064\n   \\]\n   So, Enrique has a total of 283,064 pages to shred.\n\n2. **Determine how many times Enrique needs to shred 6 pages at a time:**\n   Since his shredder can handle 6 pages at a time, we divide the total number of pages by 6.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{283,064}{6} = 47,177.3333\\ldots\n   \\]\n   Since Enrique can't shred a fraction of a time, we round up to the next whole number. This means he needs to shred 47,178 times to ensure all the pages are shredded.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{47178}\n\\]",
